Fix \(\epsilon>0\), a compatible input \((q_S,q_0)\in\mathcal C_{\epsilon}(\mathcal G,T_0)\), a target cell \((x,y)\in\mathcal I\), and \(\eta>0\). Let \((M,\mathcal R,U_0)\in\mathfrak R_{\epsilon,\eta}^{\circ}(\mathcal G,T_0;q_S,q_0)\), so the represented baseline lies in the exact fiber \(\mathfrak F_{\epsilon}(\mathcal G,T_0;q_S,q_0)\), the declared state space of \(U_0\) is exactly \(\mathcal J_0\), and \(u_j\ge\eta\) for every \(j\in\mathcal J_0\). All following vectors and inner products are indexed only by \(\mathcal J_0\). Then \(q_S(v)=(u^{\mathsf T}a_v)/(u^{\mathsf T}a_+)\), \(q_0(t)=u^{\mathsf T}b_t\), and \(\psi_{x,y}(M)=u^{\mathsf T}h_{x,y}\). If \(h_{x,y}
otin\Gamma_{(M,\mathcal R,U_0)}\), choose \( eta\in\Gamma_{(M,\mathcal R,U_0)}^{\perp}\subseteq\mathbb R^{\mathcal J_0}\) with \( eta^{\mathsf T}h_{x,y}
e0\). For every \(	au\) satisfying \(0<\lvert	auvert\le\eta/(2\lVert etaVert_{\infty})\), the construction \(u^{\pm}=u\pm	au eta\) yields graph-compatible triples \((M_1,\mathcal R_1,U_0),(M_2,\mathcal R_2,U_0)\in\mathfrak R_{\epsilon,\eta/2}^{\circ}(\mathcal G,T_0;q_S,q_0)\). Hence \(M_1,M_2\in\mathfrak F_{\epsilon}(\mathcal G,T_0;q_S,q_0)\), \(\operatorname{Obs}_{T_0}(M_1)=\operatorname{Obs}_{T_0}(M_2)=(q_S,q_0)\) exactly, and \[\psi_{x,y}(M_1)-\psi_{x,y}(M_2)=2	au eta^{\mathsf T}h_{x,y}
e0.\] Because \(\mathbf 1\in\Gamma_{(M,\mathcal R,U_0)}\), both perturbed vectors remain normalized, and for every \(j\in\mathcal J_0\), \(u_j^{\pm}\ge u_j-\lvert	auvert\lVert etaVert_{\infty}\ge\eta/2>0\). Thus their declared state space remains exactly \(\mathcal J_0\); positive selection normalizers are preserved, and \(\lVert h_{x,y}Vert_{\infty}\le1\) keeps both scalar queries in the probability range.

